original_question:
Write a Verilog module named `bin_to_decimal` that converts a 16-bit binary input `B` into a 5-digit Binary Coded Decimal (BCD) output `bcdout`. The module should have the following interface:

```verilog
module bin_to_decimal(
	input [15:0] B,
	output reg [19:0] bcdout
);
// ... module body ...
endmodule
```

Your implementation should correctly perform the conversion from the 16-bit binary value to its equivalent 5-digit BCD representation.
